    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 163\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 4492, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  in  relation  to ordering a study and report on a proposed\n      extension of the Long Island Motor Parkway trail, a  part  of  the\n      Brooklyn Queens Greenway, east from Winchester Boulevard to Little\n      Neck  Parkway  in  the  county  of  Queens to the trailhead of the\n      planned Motor Parkway trail in the county of Nassau; and providing\n      for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the Office of Parks, Recreation  and  Historic\nPreservation  (OPRHP) and the Office of Mental Health (OMH) to conduct a\nstudy of the costs, traffic  impacts  and  environmental  impacts  of  a\nproposed  extension of a bicycle-pedestrian trail from eastern Queens to\nthe trailhead of the Long Island Motor Parkway  Trail.  In  effect,  the\nbill would call for an environmental impact statement for a project that\nis not currently contemplated by OPRHP and for which there are no appro-\npriated funds.\n \n  In  addition  to  the  fact  that  OPRHP  and OMH would be required to\nconduct a feasibility study of a project on  a  speculative  basis,  the\ncompleted study would have to be delivered within one year of the effec-\ntive date of the bill.\n \n  I  support  the laudable intent of this legislation and urge the spon-\nsors to revisit this project in the  context  of  state  budget  negoti-\nations.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
